  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "y[n] = x[n] * w[n], one multiplication for each sample",
        "The window falls to nothing at both ends, thus the block meets itself",
        "Without it, one tone smears across the whole result"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "w[n] = a0 - a1*cos(t) + a2*cos(2*t) - a3*cos(3*t), with t = 2*pi*n/(size-1)",
        "Hann, Hamming, Blackman and Blackman-Harris differ in those four numbers alone",
        "The divisor is size-1, thus the last value equals the first and the shape is symmetric"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What you trade",
      "items": [
        "A wider main lobe hides a tone that stands close by",
        "Higher side lobes hide a weak tone that stands far away",
        "Tukey and Kaiser do not fit the sum and are worked out on their own"
      ]
    }
  ]
